        "fr-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "5bd45597-f471-3101-9b42-2b15a4a607d9",
                "word": "surtourisme",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "d0f80885-ce56-4494-9e82-db5d5a061673",
                        "entry_id": "5bd45597-f471-3101-9b42-2b15a4a607d9",
                        "tags": [],
                        "form": "sur-tourisme"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "f137737c-ea64-3c71-8de9-e221499b5934",
                        "entry_id": "5bd45597-f471-3101-9b42-2b15a4a607d9",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Situation dans laquelle il est jugé qu’un trop grand nombre de touristes visitent un lieu et le dégradent."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "eb2ffd7e-1087-4f8a-9b00-80ed5e0c4f2b",
                                "sense_id": "f137737c-ea64-3c71-8de9-e221499b5934",
                                "text": "En effet, l’UNESCO a menacé de retirer Dubrovnik de la liste du patrimoine mondial de l’humanité si les autorités n’y faisaient pas diminuer le nombre de touristes ; des habitants de Venise ont manifesté contre le surtourisme et en particulier contre les navires de croisière ; les iliens de l’archipel des Hébrides, en Écosse, ont lancé un appel à l’aide car l’afflux de touristes sur les routes les empêchait d’aller faire leur courses et de rendre visite à leurs parents."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "bd8a4e08-b737-42ce-9372-57d9cc8b122c",
                                "sense_id": "f137737c-ea64-3c71-8de9-e221499b5934",
                                "text": "La France n’est pas encore dans le surtourisme, mais, si on ne bouge pas, on y sera dans trois ou quatre ans. Le sujet est très grave : 80 % des touristes visitent les sites culturels parisiens le long de la Seine, et on est proche de la saturation."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "10c935bb-d575-42bd-a306-1677a9b73498",
                        "source_entry_id": "5bd45597-f471-3101-9b42-2b15a4a607d9",
                        "source_sense_id": "f137737c-ea64-3c71-8de9-e221499b5934",
                        "target_lang_word": "Übertourismus",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Übertourismus",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "da6756b4-10f8-375c-9bc7-a3f3438f6b88",
                                        "entry_id": "e0848322-346a-32d7-9ac1-21f35f91f78f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "übermäßiger Tourismus, der das Leben der Einheimischen erheblich beeinträchtigt"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0e7e6bc6-1f5d-4210-abb1-784aa559ae51",
                                                "sense_id": "da6756b4-10f8-375c-9bc7-a3f3438f6b88",
                                                "text": "„In Italien, Spanien und Portugal sind Tausende Menschen gegen Übertourismus auf die Straße gegangen – einige griffen zu ungewöhnlichen Protestmitteln.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "a0bf2655-68b6-476e-9ae4-2d82d3e926ed",
                        "source_entry_id": "5bd45597-f471-3101-9b42-2b15a4a607d9",
                        "source_sense_id": "f137737c-ea64-3c71-8de9-e221499b5934",
                        "target_lang_word": "overtourism",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "overtourism",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8493bc8b-2520-31fa-9649-96f5629836d1",
                                        "entry_id": "89d5b578-4001-3251-aeec-cb67d4efcaa9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Excessive tourism."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a5cc06ac-88bd-4edd-b4c6-eaab9bcbdf38",
                                                "sense_id": "8493bc8b-2520-31fa-9649-96f5629836d1",
                                                "text": "As evidenced in the overtourism concept, residents may become resentful of the intrusions of visitors and visitors' impacts on their ways of living (Figure 9.2). Thus, it is essential that residents are involved and have a strong say […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6ca51109-b103-4df6-9f01-2df1076d0922",
                                                "sense_id": "8493bc8b-2520-31fa-9649-96f5629836d1",
                                                "text": "If tourism is a capitalist phenomenon, overtourism is its demented late-capitalist cousin: selfie-stick deaths, all-you-can-eat ships docking at historic ports, stag nights that end in property crimes, the live-streaming of the ruination of fragile natural habitats, et cetera."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2d4dcb94-34a3-4c8e-a54d-c10b97200574",
                                                "sense_id": "8493bc8b-2520-31fa-9649-96f5629836d1",
                                                "text": "After years in the making, Venice will on Thursday begin charging day trippers to enter the city in an effort to protect the Unesco world heritage site from the effects of over-tourism."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "61f4a2cc-85b3-43b9-b577-3587c194e084",
                                                "sense_id": "8493bc8b-2520-31fa-9649-96f5629836d1",
                                                "text": "In Barcelona, the center of recent protests against overtourism in European cities, demonstrators carrying signs reading “Tourists go home” and “Tourism is stealing from us” marched down the city’s so-called Golden Mile, a street flanked by luxury boutiques and high-end hotels, spraying visitors with water outside a Louis Vuitton store."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
